            "review_title": "Review at Cà-rem",
            "review_text": "Amanda D\nVancouver, Canada54 contributions\n1\nDelicious!\nJun 2016 • Friends\nA great treat in Saigon! \nAs described in other reviews, it's a scoop of yummy coconut ice cream, made with coconut milk, topped with just a bit of peanuts, sticky rice, pumpkin, corn and toasted coconut, served in half a coconut, so there's fresh coconut meat underneath to enjoy as well. And a side drink of coconut water. At 35,000 VND, it's a splurge by Vietnamese standards but well worth the treat. \nIt's definitely a trendy spot for local young people, busy on a Tuesday night with an air conditioned indoor eating area. The tables and stools are wooden but tiny. A fun and tasty experience.\nRead more\nWritten June 15, 2016",
